+  // Fil-C: pizlonate everything.  The Fil-C pipeline (KillUB, the Fil-C early
+  // simplification and inlining pipeline, C++20 coroutine lowering, the
+  // FilPizlonator on every path, and the OptimizerLast
+  // DeleteRedundantPollchecks) is owned by LLVM's RegisterFilPasses
+  // (llvm/lib/Passes/RegisterFilPasses.cpp) and registered here with
+  // IsRust=true, exactly like clang/lib/CodeGen/BackendUtil.cpp registers it
+  // with IsRust=false -- so rustc pizlonates exactly like Fil-C clang does.
+  // IsRust disables the whole pre-pizlonation simplification and inlining
+  // pipeline by default because it miscompiles rustc-shaped IR (see
+  // RegisterFilPasses.cpp; FILCRUST_FILCINLINE in the environment re-enables
+  // it).  The callbacks run
+  // on every path through this function -- O0 via buildO0DefaultPipeline,
+  // the prepopulated per-module/ThinLTO/fat-LTO pipelines, and (via
+  // FilCAddPipelineStartPasses in the NoPrepopulatePasses branch below) the
+  // no-prepopulate pipeline -- so every module that rustc compiles gets
+  // pizlonated, at every optimization level.
+  RegisterFilPasses(PB, nullptr, true);
+
