+// Fil-C requires pizlonating all code and rejects the naked-asm stack-probe
+// helper (the Fil-Pizlonator only allows module-level asm of specific
+// .filc_* forms), and Fil-C clang never probes stacks.  The inner cfg must
+// mirror the Fil-C x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu target spec exactly (the only
+// Fil-C target, which sets StackProbeType::None), so that the exclusion
+// matches the set of targets rustc actually configures without stack probes.
+#![cfg(not(any(
+    windows,
+    target_os = "cygwin",
+    all(target_arch = "x86_64", target_os = "linux", target_env = "gnu")
+)))]
 // All these builtins require assembly
 #![cfg(not(feature = "no-asm"))]
 // We only define stack probing for these architectures today.
